FUN_1000_35a7 + FUN_1000_3920 (frame/event scheduler pump): DGROUP near-offset base-loss + dropped CF.

FUN_1000_35a7 is the frame/vsync POLL that FUN_1000_38cc spins on -- the target of the reloc-section
0x1d8 method vector DGROUP:0x40a (= 0xf69:0x3f17), newly recovered by seeding it in SeedServiceVecs.java.
It pumps the cooperative event queue (DGROUP near-offset linked list at 0x18e0/0x18e2/0x18e4/0x18e8) and
returns status in the x86 CF via stc/clc+lret: CF=1 when the frame semaphore [0x3e00] is set OR the event
queue is empty ([0x18e4]==0xffff).  Ghidra typed the DGROUP node NEAR OFFSETS as host int*/int** (base-loss
+ 4-byte pointer scaling), compared the 0xffff empty-queue sentinel against a host address (&DAT_2000_bfff),
and dropped CF.  Reconstruct faithfully with 16-bit DGROUP near offsets (base g_mem+0x1c000) per asm
0x135a7..0x1363f, and thread CF through the shim global g_fist_cf (native_main.c).  On the intro path
FUN_1000_3446 built an empty queue so the fast path returns CF=1 at once; the event-dispatch block is
reconstructed but not exercised until events are queued.

FUN_1000_3920 is the cooperative-yield trampoline 35a7 calls first (asm 0x13920: `push [DGROUP:0x310];
ljmp far [DGROUP:0x48]`).  The far target 0000:0199 (FUN_0000_0199) pops the pushed word into the low half
of the far pointer [DGROUP:0x3a:0x3c], `call far [0x3a]`, then `ljmp 0xf69:0` (0xf690 = a bare `ret`) so
the trampoline returns to 35a7:135b1.  Net effect: [0x3a].low=[0x310]; call far [0x3c]:[0x310]; return.
Ghidra lost the SS->DGROUP base (rendered [DGROUP:0x48] as static-SS host word DAT_2000_bad8) and the
push/pop; reconstruct faithfully.

The DGROUP:0x40a vector itself is installed at boot by the loader/CRT role (native_main.c
fist_install_dgroup -> fist_apply_reloc_section(0x1d8,1)); the engine's own 0x1d8 sites bail (f842 on bx==0)
or clear (f860).  See docs/stage1.md.
